 "content": "# Continual-ARC pattern: overlay intersection

A useful ARC transformation to recognize: an input may contain two equal-sized binary/color masks separated by a solid-color divider (sometimes side-by-side, sometimes stacked). Align corresponding cells, keep only locations where both masks are nonzero, and recolor those overlaps with the output color (often 2); elsewhere output 0. The demonstration for task-6e926b58 was 13x21 with two 13x10 masks separated by a 7 column; output was 2 exactly where the left mask had 1 and right mask had 9. The test was 27x3 with top 13 rows of 4s, row 13 a separator of 3s, and bottom 13 rows of 5s; output was a 13x3 grid marking intersections of 4 and 5 as 2.

When applying, verify divider orientation and exact mask dimensions; discard divider, align the masks, and compute cellwise nonzero AND."
